; P3 gate: a PCM SE takes the voice as an FM or PSG effect takes its channel
; (driver.md §2.5). A BGM pcm1 part rolls (:keyon) under a :vel swell; an SE
; on the same voice at f40 brings its own :vel envelope and :vol. The song's
; part plays on unheard into the voice's ghost; at the effect's end (f55) the
; voice's state is the song's again — its levels, its binds — but not its
; sound: the loop the effect cut is not started again, and the part sounds
; from its next note (f60; on PAL f100, its f50 note fell under the effect),
; rolling under its swell, as if the effect had never fired
; (p3-se-pcm-macro-twin). Host-driven (auto-start off).
(def-score :pcm-voices 2)
(def-pcm pad :file "pad.wav" :loop-start 9ms :loop-end 36ms)
(def-pcm blip :file "blip.wav")

; track 0 (bgm-pcm): a looping pad that rolls on sixteenths.
(pcm1 pad :tempo 120 :mode loop :oct 4 :len 2
  (macro :step 1/16 :keyon [1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1]) (macro :vel (linear 8..15 :len 4f))
  c c c c)

; the effect (track 1): a blip on pcm1 with its own decaying :vel and :vol, no roll.
(def-se hit (pcm1 blip :oct 5 :len 8 :vol 12 (macro :vel [15 12 9 6 3]) c))
